2026-08-15 14:35:40,917 1053867 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'FIRMWARE DEFECT FOUND 2026-08-15. The RX-window clamp does not guarantee the fit it exists to guarantee, and the case it misses is reported as a successful repair.\n\nclampRxWindow (MtConfigClamp.h:69-77) ends with:\n    return room < RX_WIN_FLOOR ? RX_WIN_FLOOR : room;\n\nWhen the room left inside the beat is below RX_WIN_FLOOR (3000), it returns 3000 - which is LARGER than the room available - so rx.win + tx.drain + RX_MARGIN_MS exceeds the beat. That is exactly the state the function exists to prevent.\n\nREACHABLE WITH VALUES EVERY BOUND ADMITS. heartbeat clamps 30000..86400000, tx.drain clamps 1000..60000. Take beat 30000 and tx.drain 26000:\n    overhead = 26000 + 2000 = 28000, which is < 30000, so the early return does not fire\n    room     = 2000\n    2000 < 3000, so the function returns 3000\n    3000 + 26000 + 2000 = 31000 against a beat of 30000\nPer the file\'s own reasoning at :55-60 the consequence is that nextBeatAt_ is already past when the sleep is entered, so the device never sleeps: 100% duty, months of battery become hours.\n\nAND IT IS REPORTED AS A REPAIR. MtConfig::reconcile() has an UNREPAIRABLE branch for the neighbouring case, but its test is txDrainMs + RX_MARGIN_MS >= heartbeatMs - 28000 >= 30000 is false - so this input takes the REPAIRED path and logs "REPAIRED rx.win 60000 -> 3000". A log announcing a repair that did not repair is worse than no log, which is the exact argument the file makes twelve lines earlier about not shrinking rx.win behind a reassuring message.\n\nTHE INTERACTIVE PATH IS SAFE. applySet refuses rx.win when v + tx.drain >= beat and refuses tx.drain symmetrically, so a person cannot set it there over the air. It is reachable through a PERSISTED RECORD or a migration - which is the path with no operator to read an error, and the reason reconcile exists at all.\n\nTHE CODE IS DEFENSIBLE; THE CLAIM IS NOT. RX_WIN_FLOOR is rx.win\'s own per-field minimum from CONFIG_FIELDS, so returning below it would produce a value the field itself rejects. The function is caught between a cross-field rule and a per-field bound and picks the field bound, which is a reasonable choice made silently.\n\nFIX, not applied - read-only on code: extend the UNREPAIRABLE treatment in reconcile() to cover room < RX_WIN_FLOOR, so the state is said aloud rather than mislabelled. The claim then needs softening too - the clamp fits it inside the beat where it can, and says so where it cannot.\n\nRecorded as verdict CONTRADICTS on config-and-persistence/rx-window-fits-beat, which the board will raise as a defect automatically.'}
