2026-08-16 11:30:53,597 1053867 DEBUG mcpp.tool CALL plan_task_notes_set args={'kind': 'note', 'text': 'DONE, AND THE BUILD IS PROVEN: pio run -e v3 SUCCESS in 31.23 s, RAM 25.8%, Flash 39.3%. Commit 6ac6dae. Four files: gen_frames.py:20 (.parent x2 -> x3), check_api_md.py:77 (x4 -> x5), rak/include/secrets.h installed (untracked, verified against every symbol this tree uses), secrets.h.example refreshed. gen_schema.py untouched - already correct. The 44 rak/v2 deletions were left unstaged; they are not mine.\n\nTHE THING I HAVE TO OWN, AND IT IS WORSE THAN THE BUG. THE BOARD ALREADY HAD THIS, IN MY OWN REPO, AND I DID NOT READ IT. docs/specs/AREAS.yaml carries a `blocker:` field, recorded 2026-08-14, that says:\n\n    "The firmware does not build. The frame generator resolves the shared schema two\n     directories up; it lives three up. Every build dies at the pre-build gate. One line\n     in rak/tools/gen_frames.py. Reproduced twice."\n\nThat is the exact fix, named to the file, with the exact off-by-one, and it says REPRODUCED TWICE. It landed in commit 1012c4b, which is MINE, from earlier in this same session. I then spent this whole exchange rediscovering it from a build failure while Peter pushed me through three rounds of "well it has to be doesn\'t it".\n\nSo Peter\'s "this should be trackable with specboard!" has an uncomfortable answer: IT WAS TRACKED. The tracking worked. The reader did not. What failed is not the board\'s coverage, it is that I did not open the file that states the one thing stopping the project before doing anything else.\n\nWHAT THE BOARD DID NOT HAVE, so the tracking was not complete either: the blocker names only gen_frames.py. It does not mention check_api_md.py:77, which was the same off-by-one and would have failed next, and it does not mention the missing secrets.h at all - which was the larger of the two and the one with no documented recovery, since platformio.ini:18 pointed at a stale example.\n\nTWO ITEMS NOW OUTSTANDING ON THE BOARD, NEITHER ACTIONED, BOTH DELIBERATELY:\n\n1. THE BLOCKER IS NOW FALSE. It says the firmware does not build; it builds. A banner that lies on the board Peter looks at is worse than no banner. Clearing it means editing the `blocker:` field in docs/specs/AREAS.yaml - db.py:282 reads it from the tracked repo\'s own corpus on import, so device owns that field - but AREAS.yaml is headed "GENERATED from the board\'s database - do not edit by hand". The one field device owns can only be set by hand-editing a file that says do not hand-edit. That contradiction is specboard\'s to resolve, not mine to route around.\n\n2. THE DEFECT ITSELF IS NOT ON THE BOARD AS A DEFECT. POST /defects/raise exists and works (area, item, does, where, effect, confidence, who, kind). I did not call it: raising triggers _export(conn), which writes docs/specs/<area>/bugs.yaml in THIS repo, and neither that file nor AREAS.yaml is in the spec attached to this task. /idiot says a finding outside scope is reported, not fixed. Reported.\n\nAND I NEARLY FILED TWO FALSE ABSENCES GETTING HERE. First I said the board had no way to raise a defect - wrong, add_defect() exists in db.py. Then I said the only POST route was /rc/item - wrong, the app dispatches on `if u.path ==` inside do_POST rather than on decorators, and there are sixteen routes. Both times my grep matched a pattern this codebase does not use, and both times "not found" came out of my mouth as "does not exist". Same class as the four false absences already recorded against me.\n\nBACK ON READONLY as of this note, per Peter: "yes you can do that then you ar back on readonly."'}
